{"id": "clm:de9302f436ee52982c46faaa602789d5b0e19219e4a66e11a7a13742b0ca665c", "type": "statement", "text": "Do not accept client-controlled JavaScript or raw query objects. Build application-owned filters with driver APIs, validate expected value types, and allowlist fields and operators. JavaScript interpolation can enable data extraction, while client-supplied objects can introduce operators even when the application uses query objects. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://portswigger.net/web-security/nosql-injection", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["$function and server-side JavaScript hardening"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/NoSQL_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b0be8e0a08166e01a52c98a3e2b08a8bd23a3848fefaebcdb402af464f89e7d7", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:326cd69f2cf926a77099453328c60ec705c7c2f2693e20f1885f6580db1cbdf7", "ev:3b77db8bf6c86a6544624c2db849c8d97d1efc1523f6bc26c02b20eb8f49c332", "ev:5e63f2be5f3f8f58c748ee3530a88f46db8067006f1dcacafcb04ca61cc4540f", "ev:95602ea853d937df037ef057e128336aa66bdc5dec5ffb9c94b69955d9c56653"]}
{"id": "clm:b5ad6f1a9b9ca634fe77f62f6ae7cacb274087300a897bf130b2e11b7665ccd4", "type": "statement", "text": "Percona's June 17, 2026 advisory describes CVE-2026-11933 in the older BSON-to-JavaScript-array conversion path: an authenticated user with read privileges and scripting enabled could trigger memory disclosure or a crash. Its upstream ticket concerns BSON wrapper ownership. This historical evidence does not establish that MongoDB 9.0's WASM engine has the same vulnerability. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-06-17)", "source_url": "https://www.percona.com/blog/security-advisory-cve-2026-9740-and-cve-2026-11933-in-percona-server-for-mongodb/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["$function and server-side JavaScript hardening"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-128125"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b0be8e0a08166e01a52c98a3e2b08a8bd23a3848fefaebcdb402af464f89e7d7", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:85b8ca10c8fd1992443c05133dea2deb556bd4e7142c6b5badedf9f0b5e5ac3a", "ev:9f9b68d5696e0de2d4362dca0dd5316aaa0eae4192b41810b55e8867c14fb115", "ev:ed8444e78f191bc57a0addae0837b6d8de90a903af2ebda169d106bf9d9a2873"]}
{"id": "clm:455c49f7a0844b13d9e3699daeb50ab5c632d3576bb3751867a645b49a230e74", "type": "statement", "text": "Prefer native aggregation expressions inside $expr over $where when they express the same predicate. Replacing $where with $expr plus $function still executes JavaScript and still requires scripting to be enabled. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/function.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["$function and server-side JavaScript hardening"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "how-to", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/query/where.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b0be8e0a08166e01a52c98a3e2b08a8bd23a3848fefaebcdb402af464f89e7d7", "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED", "evidence_ids": []}
{"id": "clm:999f73f57b007606156c514e0f89685914b128f85ef6a64b178f2493fadfaf38", "type": "statement", "text": "Prefer native aggregation expressions, including through $expr, over $where when they express the same logic. If custom JavaScript is necessary, MongoDB prefers $function over $where; moving JavaScript under $expr does not eliminate JavaScript execution. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/function.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["$function and server-side JavaScript hardening"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "how-to", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/query/where.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b0be8e0a08166e01a52c98a3e2b08a8bd23a3848fefaebcdb402af464f89e7d7", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:7892f516ff27a803574ff19148f47767d65334706621b35f3551610e88ebc623"]}
{"id": "clm:c542121aac8a7e4adee400ff19b98bee31b0cff39009c6efc0065c610c586ee2", "type": "statement", "text": "$function uses a body containing JavaScript, an args array, and lang: \"js\" to define a custom aggregation expression. MongoDB recommends it only when native pipeline operators cannot fulfill the application's needs, because JavaScript execution may reduce performance. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/function.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["$function and server-side JavaScript hardening"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/query/where.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b0be8e0a08166e01a52c98a3e2b08a8bd23a3848fefaebcdb402af464f89e7d7", "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED", "evidence_ids": []}
{"id": "clm:848c0619373c80dd87c1704bbfa0e6a0e3dadcc3c547736a0fab5c62ea9d2635", "type": "statement", "text": "$where itself cannot use indexes, and a $where-only filter requires a collection scan. If it cannot be removed, include ordinary selective predicates: MongoDB evaluates non-$where conditions first, and those conditions may use indexes. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/query/where.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["$function and server-side JavaScript hardening"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b0be8e0a08166e01a52c98a3e2b08a8bd23a3848fefaebcdb402af464f89e7d7", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:625a2fb19d15c3cecbd4893580aeb00031badd27806df176fa9134f01bf3f11e"]}
{"id": "clm:398a953124cb38d7d5244a48e05d320a4b8550ae68dd021054e04fe507511284", "type": "statement", "text": "If the application does not require $where, $function, $accumulator, or mapReduce, disable server-side scripting on mongod and mongos using security.javascriptEnabled: false or --noscripting. Inventory application queries before disabling because dependent operations will fail. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/server-side-javascript.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["$function and server-side JavaScript hardening"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/function.md", "https://www.percona.com/blog/security-advisory-cve-2026-9740-and-cve-2026-11933-in-percona-server-for-mongodb/", "https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/NoSQL_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b0be8e0a08166e01a52c98a3e2b08a8bd23a3848fefaebcdb402af464f89e7d7", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:011d960e6add91aa478b52a8373f90cb64b976f89eff3e5ca71164e0e4df60cb", "ev:8f14410e48884ce6feb47e8a3f5353e5528fd7e0d59b8b286a5b6d2c588d2d8d", "ev:b957a9b9563b66e4ea94d62ea8cc9ca6f591827887ef6391e7a99b1a85e4ecef"]}
{"id": "clm:611b34bd53c5b48556ccdb60d037f7c34ff464223e39d75cf7ab90cc2104d2e8", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB 8.0 deprecated $function, $accumulator, and $where and logged warnings when they ran; deprecation did not mean immediate removal. (high confidence) (verified as of 2024-10-23)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/core/server-side-javascript/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["$function and server-side JavaScript hardening"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/community/forums/t/why-is-function-deprecated-in-mongod-8-0/291213"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b0be8e0a08166e01a52c98a3e2b08a8bd23a3848fefaebcdb402af464f89e7d7", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2a798d36a2a210a299ca029204a09a30a9271cce19ae55251791ae6dea2b77ae", "ev:9c8eb9dbaf0ca419e21229931baf1ec20884fca3e8dd58cb64d5086de7e989cc"]}
{"id": "clm:3b5d5d991e7c9cc7460dc188d32b0c1e64e6c69860ca34444ebdc8c0f8dea0ce", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB 9.0 reverses the MongoDB 8.0 deprecation of $function, $accumulator, and $where. Do not carry an unqualified \"deprecated since 8.0\" recommendation into 9.0 guidance. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-09-28)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/release-notes/9.0.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["$function and server-side JavaScript hardening"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b0be8e0a08166e01a52c98a3e2b08a8bd23a3848fefaebcdb402af464f89e7d7", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:156212ba2e6a5ca1b3e9e965863e7cf1483733b406f2e9106e8510066270ebfd"]}
{"id": "clm:de92343fa4b2c142ba050d700e1c2a1b0647ad6f0ed438e666e8de92e6dd0414", "type": "statement", "text": "Starting in MongoDB 9.0, ppc64le mongod and mongos binaries omit the JavaScript engine: $function, $accumulator, $where, and mapReduce fail there. A configuration switch cannot restore support; rewrite the operations or use an architecture with a JavaScript engine. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/server-side-javascript.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["$function and server-side JavaScript hardening"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/release-notes/9.0-compatibility.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b0be8e0a08166e01a52c98a3e2b08a8bd23a3848fefaebcdb402af464f89e7d7", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2b8cf4e2c738865cca270aaa4da0c6ceda8635cf434129096d1aea21333b54e7"]}
{"id": "clm:87554157758303cebed5deaf8b398f42d2d73a615f460aa73a215080963f0408", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB 8.0 deprecated $function, $accumulator, and $where and logs warnings when they execute. MongoDB 9.0 reverses that deprecation and re-enables these functions using a WASM-based engine; a blanket claim that they remain deprecated in every version after 8.0 is incorrect. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-09-28)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/core/server-side-javascript/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["$function and server-side JavaScript hardening"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/release-notes/9.0.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b0be8e0a08166e01a52c98a3e2b08a8bd23a3848fefaebcdb402af464f89e7d7", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:156212ba2e6a5ca1b3e9e965863e7cf1483733b406f2e9106e8510066270ebfd", "ev:9c8eb9dbaf0ca419e21229931baf1ec20884fca3e8dd58cb64d5086de7e989cc"]}
{"id": "clm:f28a168661acf78d3ef818a9670211f5875bf054e9106193f002ea25659c323a", "type": "statement", "text": "Starting in MongoDB 9.0, server-side local Date operations use UTC instead of the mongod host time zone. Review $function date logic before upgrading; use native date operators with an explicit timezone, or explicit UTC JavaScript methods when UTC is intended. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/server-side-javascript.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["$function and server-side JavaScript hardening"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/release-notes/9.0-compatibility.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b0be8e0a08166e01a52c98a3e2b08a8bd23a3848fefaebcdb402af464f89e7d7", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:06e86ed8e7a9f59aa6c79ffa0352a5af772b037c006fcd384cb7114d22336e78"]}
{"id": "clm:74d70d1e8140479c497610b1a191f0d645487a76910b081d4bb338a7379ed30a", "type": "statement", "text": "Disabling JavaScript does not eliminate NoSQL operator injection. Non-JavaScript operators such as $ne or $regex can still change filter semantics if the application accepts unvalidated query structures; field, type, and operator validation remains necessary. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://portswigger.net/web-security/nosql-injection", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["$function and server-side JavaScript hardening"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/NoSQL_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b0be8e0a08166e01a52c98a3e2b08a8bd23a3848fefaebcdb402af464f89e7d7", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6f9c46ea6975c935657e1ac02a25b03e1b889ddac2595bd2fa41d1b1064b9e93", "ev:ad59d8ed2abe0f34d01d9eba07bf9d16c3ef25ddd3213a5ea90a2527cc9dd274", "ev:ca65dbc368d295368aabe2199f6fcb1e29d909e0b575e1e9e6a39efceb4c17c3"]}
{"id": "clm:c8719dd2b7bcf739410bd00debd82e07d0708caa124254297b2c01f6d7834ac1", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB attributes stronger sandboxing and isolation in 9.0 to its WASM-based JavaScript engine. This is an engine-hardening claim, not evidence that accepting untrusted query operators or JavaScript bodies becomes safe; application input validation is still necessary. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/release-notes/9.0.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["$function and server-side JavaScript hardening"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/release-notes/9.0-compatibility.md", "https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/NoSQL_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b0be8e0a08166e01a52c98a3e2b08a8bd23a3848fefaebcdb402af464f89e7d7", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:156212ba2e6a5ca1b3e9e965863e7cf1483733b406f2e9106e8510066270ebfd", "ev:7fd926a512f4de582d425501aadc2560fa75e52a95b365b41f962ef685359b8e", "ev:c6a0930510fcbd18019eb24b656701ce29299a0cb02ae36947b9b3a3d4269553"]}
{"id": "clm:1c1914a100c3b58b9d0f0b439c83a6f4069b6f9fba760405d097eda4aeecb7cb", "type": "statement", "text": "A 2024 community discussion reports workloads where custom JavaScript outperformed native aggregation rewrites, including IP transformations. Treat these as workload-specific reports, not a transferable benchmark or proof that JavaScript is universally faster. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/community/forums/t/why-is-function-deprecated-in-mongod-8-0/291213", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["$function and server-side JavaScript hardening"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b0be8e0a08166e01a52c98a3e2b08a8bd23a3848fefaebcdb402af464f89e7d7", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:35770f486355aa70b78403691bcf7e1eb3e1ce37f85b3c0dbadc44529d72c98b"]}
{"id": "clm:b222577f78969da9665c07d69ee96190dda651ce328c1132c1b60b767e0337a0", "type": "statement", "text": "$function requires server-side scripting, which MongoDB documents as enabled by default. Do not assume installation defaults have already disabled JavaScript; inspect the configuration of the deployed version. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/function.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["$function and server-side JavaScript hardening"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b0be8e0a08166e01a52c98a3e2b08a8bd23a3848fefaebcdb402af464f89e7d7", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:011d960e6add91aa478b52a8373f90cb64b976f89eff3e5ca71164e0e4df60cb"]}
